The combination of three charges in series
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{1}{C}=\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\frac{1}{C_{2}}+\frac{1}{C_{3}} \\
\frac{1}{C}=\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{6} \Rightarrow C=\frac{6}{4}=1.5 \mu \mathrm{F}
\end{array}
$$
The charge of this circuit
$$
\begin{array}{l}
q=C V=1.5 \times 120 \\
q=180 \mu \mathrm{C}
\end{array}
$$
The potential difference across the $3 \mu \mathrm{F}$
$$
q=C V
$$
$$
V=\frac{q}{C}=\frac{180}{3}=60 \mathrm{V}
$$
